{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum","id":1531531,"title":"Resonant Condition and the Spirit Arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-26T12:09:46-08:00","id":1531531,"title":"Resonant Condition and the Spirit Arcanum","content":"Hey everyone.<br /> I'm playing a Thyrsus with Spirit 2, but until recently I've been too intimidated by the inaccessibility of the Spirit Arcanum to really delve into it. Now that I'm trying to understand how to proactively use it in-game, I came across a few things I'm having a hard time wrapping my head around and would love to hear your thoughts about them:<br /> <br /> 1. Channel Essence seems to suggest some elements of the Fallen World have the Resonant condition and some don't, but isn't everything around us Resonant to some Spirit or other? The condition seems to be tagged to a specific Spirit, but Channel Essence seems to regard it as an attribute of the elements themselves.<br /> <br /> 2. Once a Mage detects a Resonant condition in the Fallen World, could he Channel Essence freely, or would it be Withstood by the Gauntlet Strength? Is Essence accessible to Mages from this side of the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> 3. The Spirit Sight description states it &quot;detects the presence and nature of the Resonance Condition and other sources of Essence&quot;. What other sources of Essence are there except for the Resonant condition?<br /> <br /> 4. Channel Essence mentions it can be used to transfer Essence into a suitable receptacle. What's considered a &quot;suitable receptacle&quot;?<br /> <br /> 5. How much Essence can be drawn from a Resonant condition? and does the drawn Essence keeps its original Resonance?<br /> <br /> 6. Could a Spirit Knowing spell be used to track down the name and/or location of a Spirit with a specific Influence, Manifestation or Numen from afar? Would you limit it to just to the nearest Spirit that fulfills this requirement or just to Spirits on the same side of the Gauntlet as the Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28028-hubhub","name":"Hubhub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T14:14:06-08:00","id":1531544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hubhub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum#post1531531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. The Spirit Sight description states it &quot;detects the presence and nature of the Resonance Condition and other sources of Essence&quot;. What other sources of Essence are there except for the Resonant condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and get to the others later, but this one is simple to answer; Werewolf details features of the world called loci (singular locus), that are to Essence as hallows are to mana.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T18:01:23-08:00","id":1531568,"title":"","content":"6- I think you could accomplish that by casting a Unveiling of Spirit as an AoE. You just need to have enough scale for the general area you think the spirit could be in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T18:28:09-08:00","id":1531571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hubhub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum#post1531531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Channel Essence seems to suggest some elements of the Fallen World have the Resonant condition and some don't, but isn't everything around us Resonant to some Spirit or other? The condition seems to be tagged to a specific Spirit, but Channel Essence seems to regard it as an attribute of the elements themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>In game and story terms, the Resonant Condition means &quot;spirits related to this phenomenon can sense and draw sustenance from its presence.&quot; I discussed it a bit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1065032#post1065032\">here</a>, if that helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Once a Mage detects a Resonant condition in the Fallen World, could he Channel Essence freely, or would it be Withstood by the Gauntlet Strength? Is Essence accessible to Mages from this side of the Gauntlet? </div> </div> </div>Essence comes from this side of the Gauntlet; Gauntlet Strength penalizes attempts by spirits in the Shadow to draw Essence. Taking Essence from across the Gauntlet as a mage would in fact be Withstood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. The Spirit Sight description states it &quot;detects the presence and nature of the Resonance Condition and other sources of Essence&quot;. What other sources of Essence are there except for the Resonant condition? </div> </div> </div>Manifested ghosts and goetia. Werewolves. Fetishes. Things that have Essence in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Channel Essence mentions it can be used to transfer Essence into a suitable receptacle. What's considered a &quot;suitable receptacle&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Something with the capacity to hold essence, such as a spirit, werewolf, mage, or the products of the Craft Fetish spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. How much Essence can be drawn from a Resonant condition? and does the drawn Essence keeps its original Resonance? </div> </div> </div>Without having Channel Essence as a rote or Praxis nor Spirit as a Ruling Arcanum, you will be limited by the fact that the spell costs 1 Mana to cast each time and only allows you to move as much Essence as your Mana/turn rating while the spell lasts, as well as the fact that you have to move the Essence into something that can hold it and your own Pattern splits that space with your Mana capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Could a Spirit Knowing spell be used to track down the name and/or location of a Spirit with a specific Influence, Manifestation or Numen from afar? </div> </div> </div>That would entail legwork better suited to the Fate Arcanum a la Serendipity; Know Spirit and Spirit Summons are the primary published toolkit for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T20:46:59-08:00","id":1531579,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time to help out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531568#post1531568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6- I think you could accomplish that by casting a Unveiling of Spirit as an AoE. You just need to have enough scale for the general area you think the spirit could be in.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you'd rule the Mage couldn't really do it from afar, unlike, say, Spirit Summons which can summon the nearest Spirit of a specific Resonance. Fair enough. But why Unveiling and not Knowing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531571#post1531571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game and story terms, the Resonant Condition means &quot;spirits related to this phenomenon can sense and draw sustenance from its presence.&quot; I discussed it a bit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1065032#post1065032\">here</a>, if that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't everything in the Fallen world Resonant by that definition? You seem to suggest only some things are Resonant, but I'm having a hard time understanding what distinguishes those things from everything else- is it a matter of intensity (e.g. candleflame isn't Resonant, but an inferno is), one of emotional investment (e.g. a regular knife isn't Resonant, but a chef's favorite knife is) or something else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531571#post1531571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would entail legwork better suited to the Fate Arcanum a la Serendipity; Know Spirit and Spirit Summons are the primary published toolkit for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>So barring Fate magic and Spirit 3, the Mage would just have to wander the Shadow or the Fallen World (and peek into the Shadow), casting Know Spirit en masse until he finds a Spirit with the specific combination of traits he seeks? Of course, I guess he could instead bargain for this information with other Spirits and Mages or maybe just research it in some old tome, but I'm wondering specifically how the Spirit Arcanum would help in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28028-hubhub","name":"Hubhub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T21:15:34-08:00","id":1531582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hubhub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531579#post1531579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't everything in the Fallen world Resonant by that definition? You seem to suggest only some things are Resonant, but I'm having a hard time understanding what distinguishes those things from everything else- is it a matter of intensity (e.g. candleflame isn't Resonant, but an inferno is), one of emotional investment (e.g. a regular knife isn't Resonant, but a chef's favorite knife is) or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were a prosaic game for simulating an alternate reality and not a storytelling game where emotion and memory are magically potent factors, yes, everything would have more or less the same baseline level of resonance. In practice, Resonant things are things important enough to draw attention to their possessing the qualities of a given type of Resonance \u2014 Inferno describes spirits as &quot;the flesh that feeling wears,&quot; and Mummy describes the Essence of a thing as the quality that you couldn't remove and still have that that (e.g. the Essence of ice is cold).<br /> <br /> Think of it in terms of symbolism: if the thing doesn't stand out enough to communicate something about itself or its environment, it's probably not Resonant enough to register for storytelling purposes without further activity. A candleflame in the right context could be fully Resonant, especially if it's given the trappings of ritual or even serendipitous framing, but an anonymous patch of dirt among many other patches of dirt in a field isn't likely to sustain an earth elemental of any notable quality nor put the local plant spirits any closer to awaking from dormancy on its own.<br /> <br /> Analogy to Yantras is probably the best way to think about it in a Mage-only context; you need to be able to <i>recognize</i> Resonance sufficient for spirits to harvest Essence from, albeit this is from the perspective of the wider world moreso than an individual magician with occult training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So barring Fate magic and Spirit 3, the Mage would just have to wander the Shadow or the Fallen World (and peek into the Shadow), casting Know Spirit en masse until he finds a Spirit with the specific combination of traits he seeks? Of course, I guess he could instead bargain for this information with other Spirits and Mages or maybe just research it in some old tome, but I'm wondering specifically how the Spirit Arcanum would help in this regard. </div> </div> </div>Spirit Summons lets you call a spirit within your sensory range by a specified type of Resonance, and Know Spirit can help you get more information from there.<br /> <br /> Having a spirit Familiar is useful for this scouting process by virtue of camouflage and the ability to cast spells through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T05:41:05-08:00","id":1531612,"title":"","content":"I mean, the idea that effective use of the Spirit Arcanum requires exploration of the Shadow and compiling information on its inhabitants hardly strikes me as a bad way to characterise those mages. It gives a sense of how they're engaged with an otherworld, and places some constraints on what is otherwise an enormous tool kit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T06:01:00-08:00","id":1531613,"title":"","content":"In the case of detecting spirits with specific abilities, a Knowing spell gives you information about something (like using one on copper and the spell telling you every property of known to material science), an Unveiling opens your senses to something (such as finding all copper in the area). In this case, you want to sense the location of specific spirits, so an Unveiling would be able to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> Regarding range, I am using <i>Detect Substance</i> as a frame of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T16:41:55-08:00","id":1531655,"title":"","content":"I think it's hard to make an argument that the Resonant Condition only counts for things that are outstanding in some way when it's given the definition of &quot;thing that falls under a spirit's Influence&quot; and &quot;if it matches the purview in some way, it has this Condition&quot; or &quot;anything matching the description of an Influence counts as tagged to that entity&quot;, with an explicit note that it's common.<br /> <br /> It almost makes me wonder if whomever was writing the relevant Spirit spells didn't quite recognise that, although other spells seem to not have such a concern so it's hard to say. It may also be possible that it really just amounts to a way of maintaining consistency in terminology towards the purpose of saying that, yes, mages can draw Essence from basically anything.<br /> <br /> In some ways that does seem like it would make them better at channelling Essence than spiritual entities tend to be, but I can see a few things that would work against that. One is that I read Channel Essence as being limited in total to moving a quantity of Essence equal to its Potency. So you can have the spell active for a week at, say, Potency 5, but across that week you'll only be able to move five points, in whichever direction. If you take in five, you have to end the spell and cast it again to actually give any of it back out again later on. It's a hassle, even before considering the fact that Gnosis determines the actual rate of transfer.<br /> <br /> The other is that Essence is an energy that mages can't do a whole lot with innately, but is still crowding out their Mana. So maybe you can pull more Essence from any random fire than a fire spirit can, but you're not really getting the benefit from it that the spirit would, and it's at the cost of space needed for the more useful energy. I think that trade off mostly doesn't favour the mage.<br /> <br /> You can potentially end up creating a scenario where spirits have access to more free flowing Essence than they would without intervention, but that might not be the best position to be in. It's like the movie Nope; you can reliably ensure that the abomination will be around if you provide food in an easier fashion than it gets by hunting, but it turns out that it's a super bad idea to make a wild animal associate you being around with food, just in case your side of the routine gets disrupted.<br /> <br /> Some werewolves might be tempted by the prospect of such a font of Essence, but I think plenty will perceive greater Renown in dealing with something that is messing up the natural ecology so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T18:09:00-08:00","id":1531661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531655#post1531655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's hard to make an argument that the Resonant Condition only counts for things that are outstanding in some way when it's given the definition of &quot;thing that falls under a spirit's Influence&quot; and &quot;if it matches the purview in some way, it has this Condition&quot; or &quot;anything matching the description of an Influence counts as tagged to that entity&quot;, with an explicit note that it's common.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out as the one making that argument that it is an argument from the perspective of <i>employing it as a player-facing tool in a storytelling game</i>, because &quot;literally everything that can be perceived is Resonant to something&quot; isn't useful just as &quot;everything has a spirit&quot; isn't helpful for visualizing the Shadow when taken exactly as written \u2014 most spiritual Influences are broad even without the note that Influences are over general rather than specific things, with specialization being an active decision from spirits that have grown powerful enough to transcend their connection to the thing that spawned them, and Werewolf has always been fairly clear that the ranks of active spirits are biased in favor of concrete phenomena over abstract concepts.<br /> <br /> The bar for being &quot;outstanding&quot; enough to be Resonant is quite low in this reading \u2014 literally just &quot;if it's important enough to have the camera focused on it or otherwise be the subject of a description, it's Resonant with the things it communicates.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In some ways that does seem like it would make them better at channelling Essence than spiritual entities tend to be, </div> </div> </div>The primary spiritual entities available for comparison get most of their Essence by stealing it from others and have legitimate concerns for the flavor of the juice, with the ability to directly draw it from Resonance being a limited function by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other is that Essence is an energy that mages can't do a whole lot with innately, but is still crowding out their Mana. So maybe you can pull more Essence from any random fire than a fire spirit can, but you're not really getting the benefit from it that the spirit would, and it's at the cost of space needed for the more useful energy. I think that trade off mostly doesn't favour the mage. </div> </div> </div>This is the main thing I keep going back to: without stockpiling fetishes your ability to freely gather Essence (which retains its Resonance and thus constrains its utility as a bargaining chip or generalized food source) runs up against the bottlenecks of your ability to store and move it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some werewolves might be tempted by the prospect of such a font of Essence, but I think plenty will perceive greater Renown in dealing with something that is messing up the natural ecology so much. </div> </div> </div>Comparisons to the idigam are hard to avoid, as well \u2014 yes, teaching perverse incentives to the local spirits is going to mess with somebody's territory, but so will discovering that spirits are not good at laundering incompatible Resonance without getting kicked out of the natural order (which is a fantastic way to maybe invite Abyssal incursions but a <i>terrible</i> way to be a master of the subtle Arts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T03:15:10-08:00","id":1531725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531582#post1531582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this were a prosaic game for simulating an alternate reality and not a storytelling game where emotion and memory are magically potent factors, yes, everything would have more or less the same baseline level of resonance. In practice, Resonant things are things important enough to draw attention to their possessing the qualities of a given type of Resonance \u2014 Inferno describes spirits as &quot;the flesh that feeling wears,&quot; and Mummy describes the Essence of a thing as the quality that you couldn't remove and still have that that (e.g. the Essence of ice is cold).<br /> <br /> Think of it in terms of symbolism: if the thing doesn't stand out enough to communicate something about itself or its environment, it's probably not Resonant enough to register for storytelling purposes without further activity. A candleflame in the right context could be fully Resonant, especially if it's given the trappings of ritual or even serendipitous framing, but an anonymous patch of dirt among many other patches of dirt in a field isn't likely to sustain an earth elemental of any notable quality nor put the local plant spirits any closer to awaking from dormancy on its own.<br /> <br /> Analogy to Yantras is probably the best way to think about it in a Mage-only context; you need to be able to <i>recognize</i> Resonance sufficient for spirits to harvest Essence from, albeit this is from the perspective of the wider world moreso than an individual magician with occult training.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per your suggestion, I guess looking at a Resonant element as an element that &quot;stands out enough to communicate something about itself or its environment&quot; is the way to go for practical purposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531582#post1531582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Summons lets you call a spirit within your sensory range by a specified type of Resonance, and Know Spirit can help you get more information from there.<br /> <br /> Having a spirit Familiar is useful for this scouting process by virtue of camouflage and the ability to cast spells through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was asking specifically about Spirit 1 and 2 spells, as my PC hasn't gotten Spirit 3 yet.<br /> Anyhow, a Spirit Familiar does indeed sound like a valuable scouting asset which is something I haven't considered before..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28028-hubhub","name":"Hubhub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T03:15:41-08:00","id":1531726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531612#post1531612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the idea that effective use of the Spirit Arcanum requires exploration of the Shadow and compiling information on its inhabitants hardly strikes me as a bad way to characterise those mages. It gives a sense of how they're engaged with an otherworld, and places some constraints on what is otherwise an enormous tool kit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does look like very flexible toolkit, but from what little experience I have with it, the amount of setup, planning and playtime needed to actually do something meaningful with it seems to be quite large compared to other Arcana and often requires the ST to actively help speed it along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28028-hubhub","name":"Hubhub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T04:11:04-08:00","id":1531727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531613#post1531613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of detecting spirits with specific abilities, a Knowing spell gives you information about something (like using one on copper and the spell telling you every property of known to material science), an Unveiling opens your senses to something (such as finding all copper in the area). In this case, you want to sense the location of specific spirits, so an Unveiling would be able to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> Regarding range, I am using <i>Detect Substance</i> as a frame of reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I re-read the section on Practices and a few of the example Unveiling spells, and I stand corrected.<br /> How about something like this?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Detect Spirit (Spirit </b></u><b>\u2022</b><u><b>)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <br /> As long as as this spell is active, the subject is automatically aware of the presence and location of Spirits of Rank [Potency] or lower within the area of effect. Supernatural effects that hide Spirits provoke a Clash of Wills.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage chooses a single Numen, Manifestation or Influence type. As long as as this spell is active, the presence and location of detected Spirits that possess the chosen Numen, Manifestation or Influence type are highlighted for the subject. This effect may be applied up to three times, further narrowing down the detectable Spirits' profile.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28028-hubhub","name":"Hubhub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T05:37:50-08:00","id":1531730,"title":"","content":"I think that based on <i>Detect Substance</i>, you could possibly be as broad or specific as you want with the default version.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could say it detects all spirits, but optionally you could detect spirits that fall within [Potency] types of Resonance. The Reach option would allow you to narrow down the search based on [Potency] Numen, Influences or Manifestations. I think Reaching once would be able to cover all 3 types with no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T02:32:11-08:00","id":1531770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hubhub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531725#post1531725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was asking specifically about Spirit 1 and 2 spells, as my PC hasn't gotten Spirit 3 yet.<br /> Anyhow, a Spirit Familiar does indeed sound like a valuable scouting asset which is something I haven't considered before..</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need any dots in spirit to take a spirit familiar, someone else can cast the familiar spell and you pay for it as a merit (either at character creation or later if you acquire it through RP).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T02:38:27-08:00","id":1531771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531730#post1531730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that based on <i>Detect Substance</i>, you could possibly be as broad or specific as you want with the default version.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could say it detects all spirits, but optionally you could detect spirits that fall within [Potency] types of Resonance. The Reach option would allow you to narrow down the search based on [Potency] Numen, Influences or Manifestations. I think Reaching once would be able to cover all 3 types with no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this not covered by the Spirit 2 arcanum attainment &quot;Spirit Eyes&quot;? Or is it designed to be used in conjunction with that to filter/highlight specific spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T08:47:58-08:00","id":1531786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531531-resonant-condition-and-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1531771#post1531771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this not covered by the Spirit 2 arcanum attainment &quot;Spirit Eyes&quot;? Or is it designed to be used in conjunction with that to filter/highlight specific spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make an Unveiling to highlight the ones that fall into the filter. It would allow them to see the ones within sensory range, whereas the AoE would highlight the ones within the scale, which might cover a wider area. Both are helpful tools to find specific spirits, the caster would need to choose which is the most convenient approach for their needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}